WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.440
Did you know that China spends more&nbsp;
on chips than it does on oil? No,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:10.260
not those chips like microchips, silicon wafers&nbsp;
that are at the center of all electronics and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:15.000
that make our world go round. These chips, by&nbsp;
the way, are at the center of rising tensions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.960
between the United States and China. This is&nbsp;
economic war. The Biden administration right&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:25.140
now is making it so that American chip makers&nbsp;
can't sell chips to China, forgoing billions of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:30.060
dollars of revenue. Usually, American presidents&nbsp;
don't want American companies to lose out on a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:33.540
bunch of money. So what's going on here? Well,&nbsp;
it turns out that a lot of Chinese companies are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:37.800
buying American microchips and then secretly&nbsp;
using them for like military things. There's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:42.120
really a blurry line between businesses and the&nbsp;
military in China. Kind of in the United States,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:47.940
too, TBH. But anyway, all of this has created&nbsp;
a situation where chips are like the new oil,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:51.600
whoever controls the microchips has&nbsp;
the geopolitical power. This is a big,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:55.680
deep story. I just made a 30 minute video on it&nbsp;
that explains everything. With lots of beautiful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:59.940
maps that are like neon colored and a lot of&nbsp;
really good reporting so go check that out.

